# Pinned bootstrap seeds.  expanded/tools/seed.sh downloads a missing seed
# binary from https://github.com/reardan/golf/releases/download/<tag>/<asset>
# and verifies its sha256 against the pin, refusing to run it on a mismatch.
#
# v1c is the frozen minimal (v1) GOLF compiler — the first rung of the ladder:
#
#     v1c  -->  seed  -->  golf2  -->  golf2'      (fixpoint: golf2 == golf2')
#
# It is not built from source in this tree.  The tree it comes from is frozen on
# the `minimal` branch, which builds it, verifies its self-hosting fixpoint and
# publishes it; see that branch's README for how to cut a release.  Bump the tag
# and the sha256 here to adopt a new one.
#
# The sha256 below is not a guess: v1 holds the STRICT fixpoint, so compiling
# the frozen self/golf.golf with boot/golf0.py and then with its own output
# gives the same bytes every time, on any machine.  Reproduce it yourself from
# the `minimal` branch:
#
#     python3 minimal/boot/golf0.py < minimal/self/golf.golf > s1 && chmod +x s1
#     ./s1 < minimal/self/golf.golf | sha256sum
#
# If a release ever disagrees with this line, seed.sh refuses to run the binary
# rather than trusting it, which is the whole point of pinning it.
#
# file  tag           asset               sha256
v1c     minimal-v1.0  v1c-x86_64-linux    36841823a4f73ca55649e957c4aee71e9cc0212d7cd1e0767e2f0a97654200c0
